Here's a small memoize I use for expensive per-object calculations. I'm a mid-level dev and I'm planning to share it with my team tomorrow, so I'd like your opinion first.
```js
const memoByRef = fn => {
  const cache = new WeakMap();
  return obj => {
    if (!cache.has(obj)) cache.set(obj, fn(obj));
    return cache.get(obj);
  };
};
```

Learning about the observer pattern at uni, so I wrote my own emitter. Tell me what you think, please!
```js
const emitter = () => {
  const subs = new Map();
  return {
    on(t, f) {
      (subs.get(t) ?? subs.set(t, new Set()).get(t)).add(f);
      return () => subs.get(t).delete(f);
    },
    emit(t, ...a) { subs.get(t)?.forEach(f => f(...a)); },
  };
};
```

